WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.435
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.471
So, it's been a big week for me.

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:10.409
My wife and I
celebrated at a restaurant.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:14.413
My wife doesn't really know
how a restaurant works.

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:15.915
Like, I worked in restaurants.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:19.352
I know the back of the house,
I know the front of the house.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.989
I know the nuances.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.223
My wife has no idea.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:27.227
For example, she always
flags down the busboy.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.462
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.830
-She's always like,
"Excuse me?"

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.332
He's like, "Yes?!"
-Oh.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:36.936
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.206
My wife doesn't know
how to talk to foreigners.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.108
Okay?

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.643
Look at how quiet it just got.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.211
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.347
I said "foreigners."
Everybody's, "Hey, guy..."

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:51.283
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:52.885
I grew up with foreigners.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.987
My father is a foreigner.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.423
My grandfather is a foreigner.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:02.728
They do not have the complete
grasp of the English language.

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.030
So you can't talk to them

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.699
like you would talk to somebody
who knows English.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.435
All right?
It's always fragmented.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:14.106
My wife,
she's asking the busboy,

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:15.975
"Can I have another
Tito's and soda?"

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:21.848
I go, "Babe, the only 'Tito'
he knows is in the back."

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.983
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.754
He's gonna go and say,
"Tito, they need you!"

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.422
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.725
And he's gonna come out with
a towel over his shoulder

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.261
and a can of soda.
"Hey!"

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:40.533
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.236
-My wife never knows
what she wants to eat.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.605
She always goes, "You go first."
I said, "All right.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.474
I'll have a New York strip
and mixed vegetables.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.942
Back to you.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:54.881
How long did you think
I was going to take?"

00:01:54.881 --> 00:02:04.891
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.894
And She gets it from her family.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:11.998
Going out with my wife's family
is a nightmare.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.433
All right? My wife comes
from a Jewish family.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.135
Do we have any Jews
here tonight?

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.570
[ Cheers ]
Perfect.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.340
You'll get this. Okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.541
I love the Jews.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.010
The Jews are very sweet people.
All right?

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.747
My wife's Jewish.
My best friend is Jewish.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.016
They're sweet people, all right?

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:32.151
I got to build them up
because now I'm gonna

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.318
rip them to shreds, right?

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:38.791
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.160
When we go out
with my wife's family,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.097
Jews, generally, are unhappy...

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.165
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:49.902
...when they go out
to a restaurant. Right?

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.238
For example,
when we go to the table,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.675
I never sit down at the table.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.311
'Cause I know
this isn't the table...

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.113
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.215
...we're gonna be
dining at tonight.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:05.685
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:11.490
There's a lot of whispering
as we approach,

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.859
particularly coming out
of my mother-in-law.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:16.596
[ Stammering ]

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:20.299
"Oh..."

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:21.668
There's always something wrong.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.502
There's a draft.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:27.607
There's a lot of traffic.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.076
The chair's screwed up.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.244
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:34.814
The chair is always screwed up.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.349
Constantly.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.616
Food's going back.

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:40.687
Food's gonna go back...
for sure.

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.921
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:45.758
Like, they think
every ingredient

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:49.762
should be listed on the menu.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.065
So when it comes out
and they don't --

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.868
You know, they're like,
"Huh? What?"

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.737
The hand goes up.

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:01.607
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:02.775
She's like, "What's this?"

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:06.412
And the waiter's like,
"That's a little cumin."

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.247
She's like, "Well, I didn't
see that on the menu."

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.449
And I'm thinking, "I don't know.

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:12.385
Maybe the chef was in the back,
and he's like,

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.120
"Eh, let me give it
a little cumin."

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.221
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:18.491
Maybe --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.959
"A little experiment tonight.
I don't know.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:25.031
Just because it's not on page 2,
I can't use it?"

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:31.237
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.806
Italians,
we don't send food back.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.641
We'll talk about it.
"How is it?"

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:36.742
"It sucks,
but what'd you expect?

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.377
We didn't make it.
All right?"

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.079
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.081
We'll try and fix it
at the table.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.716
"Give me the pepper and the oil.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.384
Let me see what I could do.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:48.453
Some rosemary.
There it is."

00:04:48.453 --> 00:04:49.889
You guys are great.
Thank you.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.223
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.223 --> 00:04:53.592
♪♪

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:55.461
-Come on, now!

00:04:55.461 --> 00:05:00.132
That's insane.

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:01.900
Sebastian Maniscalco!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.538
